\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Ye humble souls that seek the Lord,
\par Chase all your fears away;
\par And bow with rapture down to see
\par The place where Jesus lay.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thus low the Lord of Life was brought,
\par Such  wonders love can do;
\par Thus cold in death that bosom lay,
\par Which trobbed and bled for you.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. But raise your eyes and tune your songs;
\par The Saviour lives again:
\par Not all the bolts and bars  of death
\par The Conqueror could detain.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. High o'er the angelic bands He rears
\par His once dishonoured head;
\par And through unnumbered years He reigns,
\par Who dwelt among the dead.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. With joy like His shall every saint
\par His vacant tomb survey;
\par Then rise with his ascending Lord
\par To realms of endless day.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

